    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d740">

                <pb facs="1477" n="1465" xml:id="pg1465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Colonel Marshall S.
                            Carter to General Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-07">7 August 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96789. Your 1258<anchor n="55" xml:id="d740-f1"/> refers. The President will make
                    no China policy statement without your prior clearance. In the meantime the
                    State Department is taking no action to draft Presidential policy statement
                    pending receipt of your suggested confidential message from President to
                    Generalissimo.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
